        "features": [
            {
                "id": "death-knight-wow:ebon-blade-wow:oath-of-the-ebon-blade-spells",
                "name": "Oath of the Ebon Blade Spells",
                "level": 3,
                "text": "The magic of your oath and your Runeforging feature (see below) ensure you always have certain spells ready; when you reach a Paladin level specified in the Oath of the Ebon Blade Spells table, you thereafter always have the spell in the Spells (All) column prepared. You also have the additional spells listed in the column matching the rune you have inscribed on your weapon, if any.\n\nOath of the Ebon Blade Spells\n\nPaladin Level | Spells (All) | Spells (Blood) | Spells (Frost) | Spells (Unholy)\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n3 | Death Grip | Vampiric Blood | Chains of Ice | Scourge Strike\n5 | Death and Decay | Spiritual Weapon | Frostscythe | Ray of Enfeeblement\n9 | Summon Undead | Leeching Strike | Remorseless Winter | Bestow Curse\n13 | Freedom of Movement | Evard's Black Tentacles | Ice Storm | Blight\n17 | Circle of Power | Bonestorm | Cone of Cold | Contagion",
                "category": "traits"
            },
            {
                "id": "death-knight-wow:ebon-blade-wow:runeforging",
                "name": "Runeforging",
                "level": 3,
                "text": "When you finish a Long Rest, you can inscribe one of the following runes on a melee weapon you are holding, or you can transfer the rune to a different weapon. Whenever you gain a level, you can replace it with a different rune.\n\n**Blood.** When you inscribe this rune on your weapon, and whenever you finish a Long Rest while the rune is inscribed on your weapon, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Charisma modifier plus your Paladin level. While you are wielding your inscribed weapon, you gain these Temporary Hit Points whenever you reduce an enemy to 0 Hit Points.\n\n**Frost.** While you are wielding your inscribed weapon, damage from your weapon attacks, Paladin spells, and Paladin features ignores Resistance to Cold damage. When you make the extra attack of the Light property and hit while wielding your inscribed weapon, you deal an extra 1d4 Cold damage.\n\n**Unholy.** While you are wielding your inscribed weapon, damage from your weapon attacks, Paladin spells, and Paladin features ignores Resistance to Necrotic damage. If your inscribed weapon has the Heavy property, the first creature you hit with it each turn takes extra Necrotic damage equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1).",
                "category": "traits"
            },
            {
                "id": "death-knight-wow:ebon-blade-wow:runic-power",
                "name": "Runic Power",
                "level": 3,
                "text": "Immediately after you cast Rune Strike, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity to gain one of the following benefits based on the rune inscribed on your weapon.\n\n**Blood.** You regain a number of Hit Points equal to the Necrotic damage dealt with your Rune Strike.\n\n**Frost.** Frost covers your weapon and shatters on impact. The target of your Rune Strike and each enemy in a 10-foot Emanation originating from the target take 2d6 Cold damage.\n\n**Unholy.** The target of your Rune Strike is cursed until the end of your next turn. The next time the cursed target makes a saving throw, it subtracts 1d6 from the roll, and the curse ends.",
                "consumes": {
                    "resource": "channel_divinity",
                    "amount": 1
                },
                "category": "traits"
            },
            {
                "id": "death-knight-wow:ebon-blade-wow:aura-of-deathly-endurance",
                "name": "Aura of Deathly Endurance",
                "level": 7,
                "text": "You and your allies have Resistance to Cold, Necrotic, and Psychic damage while in your Aura of Protection.",
                "category": "traits",
                "grants": {
                    "defenses": {
                        "resist": [
                            "cold",
                            "necrotic",
                            "psychic"
                        ]
                    }
                }
            },
            {
                "id": "death-knight-wow:ebon-blade-wow:runic-mastery",
                "name": "Runic Mastery",
                "level": 15,
                "text": "You can invoke the power of the rune inscribed on your weapon. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest. The effect depends on the rune you have inscribed.\n\n**Blood.** When a creature hits another creature you can see within 10 feet of you with an attack roll, you can take a Reaction to reduce the damage the target takes by your Paladin level. You then lose a number of Hit Points equal to your Paladin level.\n\n**Frost.** When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one attack with an exhalation of frost magic in a 30-foot Cone. Each creature in that area makes a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC. A creature takes 8d6 Cold damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n**Unholy.** When you cast Summon Undead, you can modify it so that the spell doesn't require Concentration. If you do so, the spell's duration becomes 1 minute for that casting, and when summoned, the **Undead Spirit** has a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to your Paladin level plus your Charisma modifier. In addition, the first time each turn the spirit hits a creature, the spirit deals extra Necrotic damage equal to half your Paladin level (round up).",
                "category": "traits",
                "uses": {
                    "max": 1,
                    "reset": "long"
                }
            },
            {
                "id": "death-knight-wow:ebon-blade-wow:aspect-of-the-horsemen",
                "name": "Aspect of the Horsemen",
                "level": 20,
                "text": "As a Bonus Action, you gain the benefits below for 10 minutes or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).\n\n**Generate Runic Power.** You can restore a use of your Runic Mastery by expending a level 4 spell slot (no action required).\n\n**Runeforging.** When you use your Runic Power and Runic Mastery features, you can choose any effect, not just the one that corresponds to the rune inscribed on your weapon.",
                "category": "bonus_actions",
                "uses": {
                    "max": 1,
                    "reset": "long"
                }
            }
        ],
        "resources": []
    }
